## 2. Hard answers (locked product decisions)

> **عربي:** قسم — 2.1 Can we inspect a closed EXE at runtime without source?

### 2.1 Can we inspect a closed EXE at runtime without source?

**Yes — via Windows UI Automation (primary), not via reading C# source.**

| Layer | Use when | Without source? |
|-------|----------|-----------------|
| **UIA / FlaUI snapshot** | Standard WinForms, many DevExpress controls | **Yes — primary** |
| **Screenshot + vision/OCR** | Owner-draw, empty Name/AutomationId | Yes — secondary |
| **Coordinate click** from screenshot boxes | Last resort | Yes |
| **ILSpy / metadata / reflection attach** | Rare deep dreams | Semi — opt-in, careful legally |
| **Process memory scraping** | Secrets, internals | **Forbidden** |

Closed EXE ≠ invisible. Same family as Inspect.exe / FlaUI / WinAppDriver. Already started.

> **عربي:** قسم — 2.2 Where does live automation run?

### 2.2 Where does live automation run?

- **Phase 1:** Vigil Desktop **on Windows** co-located with the EXE (LAN SQL apps usually live there anyway).  
- **Later dream:** Remote Windows worker / RDP session agent so Mac users can still drive a lab PC.  
- **Not:** pure browser-only control of WinForms (no TDS-like socket for HWND from the web).

> **عربي:** علاقتها بـ Vigil Browser

### 2.3 Relationship to Vigil Browser

| | Vigil Browser | Desktop EXE Runtime |
|-|---------------|---------------------|
| Tools prefix | `browser_*` | `app_*` |
| Tree | DOM | UIA |
| Preview | iframe / BrowserView | External window + Vigil panel (dream) |
| Screenshot | Yes | Must add |
