## 7. Screen discovery engine (the “no docs” brain)

> **عربي:** قسم — 7.1 Screen map model

### 7.1 Screen map model

```text
ScreenMap {
  appId, exePath, capturedAt
  windows: [{ title, automationId?, controlsSummary[] }]
  menuPaths: [{ path: ["ملف","تقارير",…], opensWindowTitle? }]
  keywordsIndex: { "مردود": [nodeIds], "excel": […] }
}
```

- [ ] Build incrementally during a session  
- [ ] Persist optional **sanitized** map to Library / local `.vigil/app-maps/` (no passwords, no row data)  
- [ ] Reuse map next time before full crawl  

> **عربي:** قسم — 7.2 Discovery algorithms

### 7.2 Discovery algorithms

- [ ] **Passive:** snapshot main window + open children  
- [ ] **Menu walk:** open each top-level menu (depth limit, skip Exit) → snapshot → close  
- [ ] **Ribbon walk:** DevExpress ribbon tabs/groups (when UIA exposes them)  
- [ ] **MDI / tab walk:** switch documents/tabs  
- [ ] **Keyword search:** normalize Arabic (ألف/أ) + English fuzzy  
- [ ] **Feature probe:** look for Button/MenuItem names matching «تصدير»، «Excel»، «طباعة»، «حفظ»  

> **عربي:** قسم — 7.3 Agent playbook (system prompt)

### 7.3 Agent playbook (system prompt)

When user asks discovery questions and an app is attached:
1. Prefer `app_search_ui` / latest snapshot before clicking randomly.  
2. If miss → `app_screen_map` or bounded menu walk.  
3. Confirm with `app_screenshot` when ambiguous.  
4. Never claim a feature exists without seeing a control or OCR hit.  
5. Speak Arabic if user did; give menu path as copyable breadcrumb.

